  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Pricing Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a pricing page?\", \"a\": \"A pricing page is the page on a website that lists what a product or service costs, usually as plans side by side with what each one includes. Most pricing pages also carry a feature comparison grid and a button for each plan.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to make a pricing page?\", \"a\": \"Start from your pricing model, then write each plan's price and billing unit, followed by its top features. Decide which plan to recommend and what each button opens. With Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, you describe the plans and Emergent builds the page and the database behind it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should pricing pages include prices or a contact sales button?\", \"a\": \"Include prices for any plan a buyer can choose without a call. Keep Contact sales for deals set per contract, like hundreds of seats or custom terms. Without a listed price, a buyer who wants a number first has to email you for one.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the best design for pricing pages?\", \"a\": \"A few plans side by side, one of them clearly recommended, with prices large enough to compare at a glance. Put the detailed grid below the cards and billing questions below that. Keep the button text the same on every card.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find pricing page examples?\", \"a\": \"Design galleries and marketing blogs collect pricing page examples by industry. Study the ones from companies that charge the way you do: by seat, by usage, or by project. Note how each handles yearly billing and where it puts the comparison grid.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free pricing page template?\", \"a\": \"Most page builders include a pricing table block, and design galleries share free layouts. A template gives you the cards but not the billing math or a record of clicks. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a page.\"}, {\"q\": \"How should a pricing page look on mobile?\", \"a\": \"Stack the plan cards with the recommended plan first and keep the billing switch above them. A wide comparison grid will not fit a phone screen. Show one plan's column at a time, with a selector at the top to switch plans.\"}, {\"q\": \"What makes good pricing page UI?\", \"a\": \"Clear order on each card: plan name, price, billing unit, then features. Use one accent color for the recommended plan and the same button style everywhere else. Prices set in different sizes on different cards read as a trick.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where does a pricing page go on a website?\", \"a\": \"Link it from the main navigation under the label Pricing, and again from the footer. After a purchase or a trial signup, send buyers to a thank you page that confirms the plan they chose.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some pricing page design ideas?\", \"a\": \"Add a cost estimate for metered products, a cost-per-visit line on memberships, or a quote form beside fixed packages for services. A small business with two or three offers can put pricing on a one page website as its own section.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
